WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.860
Ethiopia is a country famous for being the
place where coffee was discovered… nevertheless,

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:14.800
Ethiopians didn’t start drinking it until
very recently.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.650
During decades, this country was among the
World’s poorest.

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:22.740
But, if you follow VisualPolitik for a long
time, you already know that Ethiopia is the

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:27.460
scenario for one of the biggest miracles of
our decade.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:35.300
In the latest decades, Ethiopia has been growing
at a 10% rate year after year.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:39.980
Fashion brands like Calvin Klein or H&amp;M have
already some big textile worshops in this

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:40.980
country.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:46.140
Lots of Chinese factories are been built at
the outskirs of Addis Abeba.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:51.680
But Chinese are not the only ones interested
in Ethiopian economy!

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:56.120
At the beginning of this year 2019, Hyunday
opened their first assembly center here.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:00.829
In other words, more and more Ethiopians are
stepping out of poverty every day.

00:01:00.829 --> 00:01:09.180
But hold on just a second because this is
not the actual Ethiopian miracle!

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:14.659
You see, til the year 2018, the economy was
doing good but the political system pretty

00:01:14.659 --> 00:01:15.659
much sucked.

00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:23.640
They had an authoritarian system similar to
that of China: one party, censorship and never-ending

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:25.549
harassment to ethnic minorities.

00:01:25.549 --> 00:01:31.490
But, beating the odds, all of this changed
from one day to the other thanks to this man

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:37.670
you see on the screen: ABIY AHMED ALI, the
brand new Ethiopian prime minister.

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:42.270
And I say beating the odds because ABIY AHMED
ALI was the last person you would imagine

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:43.670
to be a reformist.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:49.049
He was an army general and a member of the
government party: The Ethiopian People’s

00:01:49.049 --> 00:01:51.159
Liberation Front.

00:01:51.159 --> 00:01:56.450
Nevertheless, as soon as this man put his
sole on the government palace, he started

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:57.650
rocking the boat.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:01.231
From one day to the other, he abolished most
of the censorship laws, banned the ethnic

00:02:01.231 --> 00:02:05.659
harassment made by the army and announced
free elections by 2020.

00:02:05.659 --> 00:02:10.679
Add to this the peace with neighbouring Eritrea
and a liberalization agenda that sounds like

00:02:10.679 --> 00:02:12.140
heaven to international investors.

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:17.840
Yes, my dear viewers, remember his name because
he has high chances to get a Peace Novel Price

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:18.840
sooner than later.

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:22.510
Definitely, he already deserves it much more
than many others who already got it.

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:26.549
But wait a minute because not everything is
sunshine and rainbows.

00:02:26.549 --> 00:02:31.279
Yes, on the paper, the intentions of this
politicians couldn’t sound better.

00:02:31.279 --> 00:02:38.560
If he achieves everything he wants, he would
become the next Nelson Mandela.

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:49.129
But, as we always say here… things are much
more complex than what they seem.

00:02:49.129 --> 00:02:52.650
Ethiopia's Amhara state chief killed amid
regional coup attempt

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:53.870
Yes, you heard this right!

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:55.849
Democratic transitions are never easy.

00:02:55.849 --> 00:03:01.540
Specially given that Ethiopia had already
a political elite enjoying lots of privileges

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:04.860
and more than 13 different tribes.

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:08.560
We are talking about an enormous country,
with more than 100 million inhabitants and

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:10.319
more than 13 languages.

00:03:10.319 --> 00:03:14.190
This is a test to ABIY AHMED real intentions.

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:18.269
With so much internal opposition and so many
ethnic tension, it is very tempting to go

00:03:18.269 --> 00:03:19.819
back to the good old dictatorship.

00:03:19.819 --> 00:03:23.419
At the end of the day, tyrants can deal with
all this things way easier.

00:03:23.419 --> 00:03:24.569
So the question now is…

00:03:24.569 --> 00:03:28.799
To what extent is ABIY AHMED willing to respect
human rights?

00:03:28.799 --> 00:03:31.420
Can Ethiopia become an actual democracy?

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:36.760
Or maybe it is too hard to resist the temptation
of becoming an authoritarian leader?

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:40.609
Today we are going to answer to all of these
questions but, before we do, let’s take

00:03:40.609 --> 00:03:43.280
a look back at the history.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:47.510
THE COUNTRY OF THE THREE REVOLUTIONS

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:49.659
Many of you associate Ethiopia with Rastafarians.

00:03:49.659 --> 00:03:53.790
As you know, Bob Marley and his accolades
practiced a religion that praised the king

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:56.110
HAILE SELASSIE, the Ethiopian emperor.

00:03:56.110 --> 00:04:01.659
No offense to the Rastafarians but Mr. SELASSIE
was an absolute monarch that ruled Ethiopia

00:04:01.659 --> 00:04:02.659
with an iron fist.

00:04:02.659 --> 00:04:06.019
An, as it happens many times with absolute
monarchs and authoritarian leaders… he didn’t

00:04:06.019 --> 00:04:07.019
die in bed.

00:04:07.019 --> 00:04:15.209
In the year 1975, the DERG guerrilla seized
power and they killed him.

00:04:15.209 --> 00:04:17.570
This was the first Ethiopian revolution.

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:27.280
DERG was a Marxist-leninist group that governed
the country during the 80s.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:33.099
In this time, they collectivized the land,
nationalized all the companies and ended with

00:04:33.099 --> 00:04:39.130
half a million of opponents.

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:46.180
Thus, Ethiopia suffered one of their worst
starvations.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:52.979
And this explains why, in 1991, after a bloody
civil war, the Ethiopian People’s Liberation

00:04:52.979 --> 00:04:54.460
Front took power.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.409
This was the second Ethiopian revolution.

00:04:56.409 --> 00:04:57.599
But make no mistake!

00:04:57.599 --> 00:05:00.000
The country didn’t become a democracy at
all.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.650
They went from die hard communism to a moderate,
China-style one.

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:08.629
This explains the good relationship between
these two countries and the economic growth

00:05:08.629 --> 00:05:09.629
they started to have.

00:05:09.629 --> 00:05:10.629
But pay attention because now Xander is going
to tell us the really interesting part of

00:05:10.629 --> 00:05:11.629
the story.

00:05:11.629 --> 00:05:12.629
But pay attention because now Eric is going
to tell us the really interesting part of

00:05:12.629 --> 00:05:13.629
the story.

00:05:13.629 --> 00:05:18.349
You see, Ethiopia has more than 100 million
inhabitans and more than 13 tribes.

00:05:18.349 --> 00:05:20.690
These tribes are not very friendly with one
another.

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:24.840
And this is why the constitution is so special.

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:29.970
To start with, Ethiopia is the only country
in the planet, alongside with Liechtenstein,

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:33.040
where the right to secesion is contemplated.

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:37.419
This means that, theoretically, each of these
9 regions you see on the map could have a

00:05:37.419 --> 00:05:39.330
referendum and become independent.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:42.080
And, of course, each of those tribes have
their own political party.

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:47.160
Most of these political parties are part of
this grand coalition called Ethiopian People’s

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:48.160
Liberation Front.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.979
And all these parties have seats in the parliament.

00:05:50.979 --> 00:05:55.020
All of this means that Ethiopian politics
are not a debate between right and left wing

00:05:55.020 --> 00:06:00.280
or conservatives versus liberals but a discussion
among different tribes.

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:02.470
And you might wonder… does this system work?

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:06.189
Can Ethiopian tribes coexist together in peace
and harmony?

00:06:06.189 --> 00:06:08.539
The answer is no way!

00:06:08.539 --> 00:06:11.509
First of all, this right to secesion is just
a theory.

00:06:11.509 --> 00:06:14.620
Each time a region wanted to secede had to
face the army.

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:17.720
And, as you can already imagine, not all tribes
are equally powerful.

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:25.389
From all those 13 ethnic groups, only 3 call
the shots: the OROMO, the AMHARA and the TIGRIYANS.

00:06:25.389 --> 00:06:30.749
The rest are suffering constant human rights
violations.

00:06:30.749 --> 00:06:36.600
This includes forced displacements, land confiscations
and, of course, massive killings.

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:40.410
For example, the Somalians living in Ethiopia
have been sufferint neverending harassment

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:41.930
from paramilitary groups.

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:45.469
And both the government as the army pretended
this never existed.

00:06:45.469 --> 00:06:47.810
Add to this the activist and journalist that
were exiled.

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:53.030
If this was not enough, Ethiopia was in permanent
war with Eritrea.

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:56.819
So yes, the economy was doing good but the
politics couldn’t go worse.

00:06:56.819 --> 00:07:00.659
And here is when the third Ethiopian revolution
came in.

00:07:00.659 --> 00:07:04.360
Let’s have a look at it, shall we?

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:07.289
TITLE: THE ETHIOPIAN ROCKSTAR

00:07:07.289 --> 00:07:11.800
I’m gonna say it again: remember this name
because he might become a peace novel price:

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:13.319
ABIY AHMED ALI.

00:07:13.319 --> 00:07:17.570
Til the year 2018, he was what we call an
‘APPARATCHIK’, this is a party man: an

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:22.370
army general that belonged to the OROMO tribe,
which, as we said before, is one of the ruling

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:23.370
ethnic groups.

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:27.159
Nevertheless, as soon as he started his administration,
he has unleashed one of the most ambitious

00:07:27.159 --> 00:07:28.610
reformist agendas in history.

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:33.040
In just one year, he has signed peace with
Eritrea, he has abolished censorship and he

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:34.419
has stopped harassment from the army.

00:07:34.419 --> 00:07:35.800
Aren’t you impressed yet?

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:37.659
So wait because I haven’t finished!

00:07:37.659 --> 00:07:40.380
He has already announced free elections for
2020, he has managed to get a woman as the

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:46.900
President and he is passing the biggest liberalizations
ever seen in Ethiopia.

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:50.740
Ethiopia to install 4G network ahead of telecoms
liberalization

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:54.150
With all of this, it is easy to understand
why he has become the new African rockstar.

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:56.559
In fact, we can already talk about the ABIYMANIA.

00:07:56.559 --> 00:08:00.419
And, believe me, everything I will say here
is not a hyperbole at all.

00:08:00.419 --> 00:08:03.400
Some religious groups already claim that he
is the Messiah.

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:10.229
In Eritrea, the former die hard enemy of Ethiopia,
there are already mothers naming their children

00:08:10.229 --> 00:08:11.270
after him.

00:08:11.270 --> 00:08:15.979
And the Ethiopian media is living a big time
renaissance.

00:08:15.979 --> 00:08:20.580
Satire is flourishing in Ethiopia

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:24.810
Brand new newspapers, brand new TV shows and
old journalist coming back to the country.

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:28.139
The pictures you see now are part of some
comedy sketch that you can find on YouTube.

00:08:28.139 --> 00:08:32.270
For the first time in history, people can
make fun of politicians, including the prime

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:33.270
minister.

00:08:33.270 --> 00:08:36.770
And it seems that next year, a Ethiopian broadcaster
will start a late night show similar to The

00:08:36.770 --> 00:08:37.770
Daily Show.

00:08:37.770 --> 00:08:42.410
All of this is pretty normal in a country
like America or UK but it is a giant step

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:43.410
here.

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:44.410
But OK, OK…

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:45.410
I know what you are going to say now!

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:47.680
It is very easy to allow free press when the
media loves you.

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:50.790
But… what happens when you have die hard
critics?

00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:55.920
Well… let’s cover that!

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:57.540
FREEDOM HAS ITS RISKS

00:08:57.540 --> 00:09:01.870
2019 has surprised Ethiopians with a terrible
draught that brought many regions back to

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:03.810
starvation.

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:07.220
Unemployment is near 20% and many young people
are in a desperate situation.

00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:10.730
If this was not enough, the old guard is far
from happy with this third revolution.

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:17.480
So look at what happened in June 2019.

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:22.050
Ethiopian army chief killed by bodyguard and
regional leader dead in coup attempt

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:27.930
The Amhara state president, Ambachew Mekonnen,
and his adviser were shot dead and the state’s

00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:30.589
attorney general was wounded in Amhara’s
capital

00:09:30.589 --> 00:09:34.790
Basically, a man from the military who belonged
to the AMHARA tribe decided to kill the governor

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:35.790
of his region.

00:09:35.790 --> 00:09:39.420
According to him, ABIY AHMED was ending all
the privileges his tribe used to enjoy.

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:42.839
So he organized a coup d’etat to separate
from the rest of the country.

00:09:42.839 --> 00:09:49.149
As you can imagine, the central government
didn’t wait a minute for retaliation.

00:09:49.149 --> 00:09:52.089
Ethiopia security forces kill alleged coup
leader

00:09:52.089 --> 00:09:54.110
But we are not talking about a military answer
only!

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:57.310
During almost 2 days, central government cut
the internet.

00:09:57.310 --> 00:09:58.440
Just like that.

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:02.860
During almost 48 hours, Ethiopians couldn’t
access to Internet.

00:10:02.860 --> 00:10:07.320
This way, they couldn’t visit any media
or any critical opinion against the government.

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:11.860
Yes, I can see what you are thinking: freedom
of speech didn’t last really long here.

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:18.360
But if you thought this was the only problem
ABIY had, you’d better think again.

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:22.040
Ethiopia referendum: Dozens killed in Sidama
clashes

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:26.360
With so much freedom, the SIDAMA tribe, one
of those groups that have been always marginalized

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:29.529
by the mainstream, decided to call for an
independence referendum.

00:10:29.529 --> 00:10:32.420
They didn’t want to become an independent
country on its own right.

00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:37.790
But they wanted to have, at least, their own
autonomous region.

00:10:37.790 --> 00:10:40.070
This is what happens when you give freedom
to the people!

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:41.839
Then, people wants to use that freedom!

00:10:41.839 --> 00:10:44.529
And in this moment is when the guys from the
Ethiopian government said.

00:10:44.529 --> 00:10:45.529
‘Oh my god!

00:10:45.529 --> 00:10:47.540
All this tribes with their referéndums are
such a pain in the ass!

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:49.870
OK, so you, Sidama guys, what do you want?...

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:50.870
A referendum?

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:51.870
OK, fine.

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:53.040
But look… can you wait at least 5 months?

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:54.550
Just 5 months?’

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:57.889
And then, the Sidama tribe said:
‘Oh, sure, five months!

00:10:57.889 --> 00:11:00.089
You totally sound like the previous governments!

00:11:00.089 --> 00:11:04.509
You talk about democracy, freedom and all
the sweet stuff but then you go fucking around

00:11:04.509 --> 00:11:06.100
again with the referendums!

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:10.050
You can take your 5 months waiting time and
stick them into your ass!!!!’

00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:13.100
And this is how violent protests emerged with
more than 30 dead people.

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:15.119
So yes, I totally understand what you are
going to say now.

00:11:15.119 --> 00:11:16.960
This Abiy Ahmed guy is more disappointing
than the latest Tarantino movie.

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:18.370
But do you know what?

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:22.610
Sometimes, history can be really beautiful.

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:26.560
Ethiopia to hold autonomy referendum for ethnic
Sidama in November

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:30.570
Yes, after so much hesitation, Abiy Ahmed
is really willing to allow that referendum.

00:11:30.570 --> 00:11:34.660
And, with Internet already working again,
it seems that freedom of speech is very alive

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:36.240
in Ethiopia.

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:39.320
For example, while we were preparing this
video, we found some English speaking Ethiopian

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:40.320
newspapers.

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:44.350
And we could find news like this one.

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:46.779
Sidama unrest death toll rises to 34

00:11:46.779 --> 00:11:48.500
I know, this is really bad news.

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:51.710
This is the kind of news that don’t make
a nice portray of the government.

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:56.750
But, precisely, the fact that an Ethiopian
newspaper can say bad things about the government

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:57.750
is, indeed, a good thing!

00:11:57.750 --> 00:11:59.370
Good luck finding something similar in China!

00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:04.730
For a better understanding, DEUTSCHE WELLE,
which is a radio similar to BBC but in Germany,

00:12:04.730 --> 00:12:07.640
has already started broadcasting in Amharic
language.

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:12.280
And look at the kind of talk shows they are
already hosting!

00:12:12.280 --> 00:12:15.860
Discussion: Country risk
They began to hear warnings that Ethiopia

00:12:15.860 --> 00:12:17.110
was endangered as a country.

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:18.110
They say this by trying to justify their fears
that a country is at risk.

00:12:18.110 --> 00:12:19.110
Again, these are not good news.

00:12:19.110 --> 00:12:21.920
And we don’t really know what are they discussing
in this talk show because we couldn’t find

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:23.520
any Ethiopian who could help us.

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:24.520
By the way, if there is some native Amharic
speaker watching this video, feel free to

00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:25.520
write us an email!

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:26.520
But the truth is that, freedom of speech really
seems to be flourishing here.

00:12:26.520 --> 00:12:27.639
And, so far, Abiy is keeping his promise of
free elections by 2020.

00:12:27.639 --> 00:12:29.540
Of course, this will not be an easy thing.

00:12:29.540 --> 00:12:33.500
First of all, Ethiopia will have to update
their census, which is extremely hard.

00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:37.019
Remember that, despite the growth, this is
still a very poor country.

00:12:37.019 --> 00:12:41.100
And the government has a lot of challenges
on the horizon, starting by the huge unemployment

00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:42.100
rate.

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:43.100
So now the question goes to you…

00:12:43.100 --> 00:12:45.029
Shall Ethiopia be able to hold those elections
by 2020?

00:12:45.029 --> 00:12:50.110
How many times will be Abiy tempted again
to go back to authoritarianism?

00:12:50.110 --> 00:12:51.250
Is Ethiopia ready for democracy?

